{
	"_doc": "Relief squads (UPDATE 09 section 4, contract C5, DECISIONS T-142; docs/gravelight/BOT_AI.md 'Relief squads'). ReliefSquad (gravelight/world/relief_squad.gd) rolls at each round start: never before from_round, never while another squad is active (max_active), never within cooldown_rounds of the last arrival, never in a boss fight, holdout or cutscene (GameState flags boss_fight / holdout / cutscene) nor a special round; then chance_per_round. A squad of size soldiers walks in from one of the map faction's edge_spawns, holds near the players for stay_seconds, then rolls survivor_chance (one stays to the round's end) and the rest try to leave: overrun_bias is each leaver's chance to be caught before the edge, so most squads are lost. A dead soldier rises after rise_delay_s as a zombie (ZombieDirector.rise_at). Soldiers' kills pay the nearest player scrip_share of the kill value (Economy.award). Every living soldier holds one slot of rounds.json max_active (ZombieDirector.actor_budget). Kits: bodies from ZombieBody.build_dressed (an existing zombie kit's clothes, living skin, the faction palette in sRGB), headgear from ZombieBody.gear_mesh; no insignia anywhere. 'marked': the faction carries the Marke (CANON 2.2: German soldiers, the Totenhafen detachment); unmarked factions rise because every squad map sits near raw substrate (2.2: 'unmarked people who die near raw substrate can still rise').",
